'''''Aloe humilis''''', also known as '''spider aloe'''<ref>{{cite web |title=Aloe humilis (Spider Aloe) |url=https://worldofsucculents.com/aloe-humilis-spider-aloe/ |website=World of Succulents |access-date=30 May 2020 |date=27 May 2020}}</ref> is a species of [[succulent]] plant  in the genus ''[[Aloe]]''. It is [[Endemism|endemic]] to [[South Africa]]'s [[Cape Province]],<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://wcsp.science.kew.org/namedetail.do?name_id=297487|title=Aloe humilis (L.) Mill., Gard. Dict. Abr. ed. 6: n.º 10 (1771).|website=World Checklist of Selected Plant Families}}</ref> and is a low growing, short stemmed aloe with small spines and which grows in dense clusters.<ref>{{cite book|author=Fred Dortort|title=The Timber Press Guide to Succulent Plants of the World: A Comprehensive Reference to More than 2000 Species|date=19 November 2014|publisher=Timber Press|isbn=978-1-60469-357-7|page=267}}</ref>

